.TH "YAMLR-DIAGNOSE" "1" "November 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
\fBValidate Native Engine Integrity & Environment Health\fR
.PP
The \fByamlr diagnose\fR command (canonical alias for \fByamlr doctor\fR) validates native engine integrity, embedded schema availability, license tier state, and local workspace health.
.PP
It performs self-tests on the borrowed document slice streaming parser, verifies OpenAPI v3 schema caches, and ensures the runtime environment is properly configured.
.PP
.SH "USAGE"
.nf
.RS
# Standard engine diagnostics
yamlr diagnose

# Verbose system check
yamlr diagnose --verbose
.RE
.fi
.SH "OPTIONS & FLAGS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB-v, --verbose\fR: Show detailed health check output, schema counts, and engine subsystem statuses.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB-h, --help\fR: Display help information.
.SH "DIAGNOSTICS PERFORMED"
1. \fBNative Engine Integrity\fR: Verifies the compiled standalone binary status, CST/AST models, and memory limits.
.PP
2. \fBSchema Cache Health\fR: Checks embedded Kubernetes OpenAPI v3 schemas (v1.21 through v1.37+) and local CRD caches.
.PP
3. \fBLicensing & Entitlements\fR: Validates license public keys, air-gapped activation status, and active tier capabilities.
.PP
4. \fBEnvironment Check\fR: Verifies read/write permissions for temporary directories and Write-Ahead Log (WAL) journal paths.
.PP
.SH "EXIT CODES"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB0\fR (\fBEXIT_SUCCESS\fR): All diagnostic checks passed; engine is healthy.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB1\fR (\fBEXIT_VIOLATIONS\fR): One or more diagnostic self-tests failed or an issue was detected.
.SH "RELATED COMMANDS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
[\fByamlr doctor\fR](yamlr_doctor.md) — Canonical doctor command.
.IP "\(bu" 2
[\fByamlr status\fR](yamlr_status.md) — Inspect workspace and license status.
